hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1161","Abu Yahya Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim, the companion of Al-Sabiri, narrated to us, Yahya bin Ishaq Al-Silahini, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Abu Bakr while he was praying, lowering the His voice, and he passed by Omar praying, raising his voice, and said: When they met with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said to Abu Bakr: “O Abu Bakr! I passed by.” “And I passed by you, O Umar, while you were raising your voice.” He said: “O Messenger of God.” I seek refuge in it. It awakens the teeth, and I seek refuge in it. He said: So he said to Abu Bakr: “Raise your voice a little,” and he said to Omar: “Lower your voice.” Abu Bakr said: I mentioned in the Book of Imamate the revelation of this verse: “And do not be loud in your prayer and do not be afraid of it.” Surah Al-Isra, verse 110."
